cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PulseAir: rigor-first evaluation of wearable air-quality forecasting"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
abstract: >-
  Research code for a thesis on wearable air-quality forecasting for an ESP32
  neckband. The pipeline covers preprocessing with imputation provenance, CTGAN
  and SMOTE augmentation with a paired-bootstrap ablation, LSTM/Transformer
  sequence models with MC-dropout uncertainty, Mondrian conformal prediction,
  SHAP attribution, an LLM risk advisory with validated output, and compression
  and ONNX export for edge deployment. Its central contribution is evaluation
  discipline: every headline metric is reported against a zero-parameter
  persistence floor, single-split results are re-tested with rolling-origin
  cross-validation, and interventions that raise an aggregate metric while
  degrading a safety-critical class are disqualified. Applied to the UCI Beijing
  multi-site data, that discipline shows no model reliably beats persistence at
  a six-hour horizon; the deployable result and the validated advisory-class
  result both come from Bangladesh data, the wearable's target population.
authors:
  - name: "Md All Shahria"
  - name: "Sanjeda Dewan Mithila"
  - name: "Anik Sarker Rudro"
  - name: "Irfanul Islam Payel"
keywords:
